    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0807" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7721</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Delegate to the Inter-Allied Council</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d655-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-14T10:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. For Secretary of the Treasury:</p>
                <p>Roumanian Minister here explains the failure of his Government to give powers to
                    any representative for signing obligations due to factional jealousies in Jassy.
                    Difficulty at last overcome to this extent that the Minister at Paris is now
                    expecting to go to America soon.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d655-f2"/> I shall see him
                    next week. Meanwhile Minister here states that nothing can be done until further
                    developments in the Russian situation. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="2" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>In full, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg578">p.
                    578</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f2" n="3" xml:id="d655-f2-content">
                <p>Doctor Angelescu presented his credentials as Envoy Extraordinary and Minister
                    Plenipotentiary, Jan. 15, 1918.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
